abstract: >
  MethaNet is a molecular-attestation system for blue-carbon methane
  diligence. It links protein-language geometry, genomic context,
  functional evidence, quality control, taxonomy, provenance, and
  validation readiness through an evidence graph. Current outputs support
  MAG/proteome screening, candidate review, and monitoring design. Calibrated
  sample and project methane-risk outputs require paired abundance,
  environmental, uncertainty, and field-validation evidence.
